[{:db/id "q-347647/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "1f89319f-0dbe-5c11-83ee-be1501623d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347647/field-1/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd" :answer/id #uuid "65086243-d80b-56bc-b9cd-f513dd77bfe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347647/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d203a9ce-bee7-5078-a0ba-971e97ffbe24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347647/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer-field/choices ["q-347647/field-1/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" "q-347647/field-1/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347647" :question/id #uuid "479b6a87-80fd-5908-88a5-89e26eabce01" :question/math-academy-id "q-347647" :question/problem "The population of maple trees in a park increases by $75$ trees every year. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the population $P(t)$ of the maples? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in years.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If the maple population is $P,$ then the rate of change of the population is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in years.\n\nSince $75$ new maple trees are added every year, the rate of change of the population of the maples is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=75.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347647/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection/cb76428d1f917b4b45ede479d93119cba3d52112ad879fc5aa3b780ab021b09d" :answer/id #uuid "68031ac3-04f3-5e00-865a-97615e114597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{200}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection/2694d4f55c1b68bbb979d7d758c79019ac2bef12b7be1f3642276fc7a2e9a010" :answer/id #uuid "f89cca23-0e2f-5924-bc2d-999e724ebd3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=200t,\\,\\,t>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection/a84cec0ca724e4d3db1a71dea9e5f830753d836544672d8272d2dea851e6ab6d" :answer/id #uuid "1890e122-73cc-5d1c-bbeb-b240c860866a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=200D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection/a9d359dc8ef9d1260d1c24c67b3805d1caa28c8b216a8c40c33ddb613b1e8c4e" :answer/id #uuid "4383e862-7286-5a9f-ac5e-f2d2ef324be7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection/ca6f58de222e73c95f5830a8ac75a82cc98417aa1c6b34c4a3bf9ebf73704a44" :answer/id #uuid "37c64e21-bff0-5ef4-b0d2-a7b1a97f80ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a60e72-6a15-5995-94e7-ec43acbd730f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79296/selection/a9d359dc8ef9d1260d1c24c67b3805d1caa28c8b216a8c40c33ddb613b1e8c4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-79296/selection/cb76428d1f917b4b45ede479d93119cba3d52112ad879fc5aa3b780ab021b09d" "q-79296/selection/2694d4f55c1b68bbb979d7d758c79019ac2bef12b7be1f3642276fc7a2e9a010" "q-79296/selection/a84cec0ca724e4d3db1a71dea9e5f830753d836544672d8272d2dea851e6ab6d" "q-79296/selection/a9d359dc8ef9d1260d1c24c67b3805d1caa28c8b216a8c40c33ddb613b1e8c4e" "q-79296/selection/ca6f58de222e73c95f5830a8ac75a82cc98417aa1c6b34c4a3bf9ebf73704a44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79296" :question/id #uuid "1a178004-fa27-5003-93fd-a25c987fab4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79296" :question/problem "A cyclist is getting $200$ meters closer to her destination every minute.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the distance $D$ (in meters) of the cyclist to her destination? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in minutes." :question/worked-solution "If the remaining distance to the destination is $D$ meters, then the rate of the change of distance is $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in minutes.\n\nSince the cyclist is $200$ meters closer each minute, the rate of change of remaining distance is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-200.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the remaining distance is *decreasing*." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79296/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79296"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-51251"] :question/worked-solution "If the pines population is $P,$ then the rate of change of the population is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in years.\n\nSince $100$ new pines are added every year, the rate of change of the population of the pines is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=100.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection/f4f4da3039fae1a77aaa48598658687d49a8fe5d3d329e6f67b07d203527a948" :answer/id #uuid "4c6f7aa9-1869-5da6-ad24-2359d4c3481c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{30t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection/e94c50c6eff282a41f4a7a7d0c3f05ec035574feac916786a9fa15dab8ef3c3d" :answer/id #uuid "9c3e0078-ed17-5ac9-8deb-824b210a6d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-30T" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection/489b4f0941f65a9559723c4f8a50c1d0196a7092109b51fdd3bfb5ef219c700d" :answer/id #uuid "2f34299d-a0f5-5838-b9b6-bfa4a2ebe106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection/be15767d610bdfde065c415b501f7659ee36660530034cf73fb4edcd1e0d4921" :answer/id #uuid "81d4ef73-8e1c-5831-93ef-9a6691697d0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=30t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection/1c65ddbfd3b1d651842ed8276464e62dfb146b066681862be74140be58aab70b" :answer/id #uuid "046ded16-6b0e-5ba2-8a3f-0efe2e8b597f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=30T" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba9eb95-5954-5c8a-9c9b-994c48b6eaf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38060/selection/489b4f0941f65a9559723c4f8a50c1d0196a7092109b51fdd3bfb5ef219c700d" :answer-field/choices ["q-38060/selection/f4f4da3039fae1a77aaa48598658687d49a8fe5d3d329e6f67b07d203527a948" "q-38060/selection/e94c50c6eff282a41f4a7a7d0c3f05ec035574feac916786a9fa15dab8ef3c3d" "q-38060/selection/489b4f0941f65a9559723c4f8a50c1d0196a7092109b51fdd3bfb5ef219c700d" "q-38060/selection/be15767d610bdfde065c415b501f7659ee36660530034cf73fb4edcd1e0d4921" "q-38060/selection/1c65ddbfd3b1d651842ed8276464e62dfb146b066681862be74140be58aab70b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38060" :question/id #uuid "3b344ee7-8693-5a88-85d4-4dd538e704ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-38060" :question/problem "An old wall clock loses $30$ seconds every week. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the difference $T$ (in seconds) between the actual time and the time shown on the clock?  Assume that the time $t$ is measured in weeks." :question/worked-solution "If the difference between the actual time and the time shown on the clock is $T$ seconds, then the rate of the change of this difference is $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in weeks.\n\nSince the difference *increases* by $30$ seconds each week, the rate of change of the difference is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=30.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38060/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353449/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "aa989acd-9827-50f5-abe0-a1c87b056cb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353449/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "67e81cb6-0174-51cd-af4e-179781d14adb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353449/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-353449/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353449" :question/id #uuid "01d0d014-2d16-55f2-87e9-0d2babf92850" :question/math-academy-id "q-353449" :question/problem "The number of completed online course enrollments increases by $18$ enrollments every hour during a promotional event. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of enrollments $E(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If the number of enrollments is $E,$ then the rate of change of the number of enrollments is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $18$ new enrollments are added every hour, the rate of change of the number of enrollments is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=18.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353449/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection/8098c7cd64237c222109ced78f7ab52ec8227eb7df79581453645e6ad6755df3" :answer/id #uuid "f8716c4b-366e-5c1e-9568-412b62246c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-kt,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection/1ed23bc37fd99604beca11cc44b3f27d697ee1656b686c34d8af4aca2e5e20e1" :answer/id #uuid "794023cb-fbe8-5468-84e7-7e80622db446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=kR,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection/e3e3eed104a50873eee0371c988a14a5aa13d4dc8c627c1bf3706edc91f452c3" :answer/id #uuid "bca2f925-fdf4-5fa2-8f63-1bfd90008886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection/f1c6414fa9fe9702586d9fb6f756561d11f74d3209742ef1dcc9daf3fe042087" :answer/id #uuid "13e19b9b-df78-5dd2-b4ed-56a0796c6d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-kR,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection/87d819b585fb71fb451e24c6dd297c8eea938de868d2679b708536cbb2b5f847" :answer/id #uuid "b39e252a-a592-5786-a6c2-195faeb3dc51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "915872be-b99f-54d4-8b43-e85e3bbc3ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79316/selection/8098c7cd64237c222109ced78f7ab52ec8227eb7df79581453645e6ad6755df3" :answer-field/choices ["q-79316/selection/8098c7cd64237c222109ced78f7ab52ec8227eb7df79581453645e6ad6755df3" "q-79316/selection/1ed23bc37fd99604beca11cc44b3f27d697ee1656b686c34d8af4aca2e5e20e1" "q-79316/selection/e3e3eed104a50873eee0371c988a14a5aa13d4dc8c627c1bf3706edc91f452c3" "q-79316/selection/f1c6414fa9fe9702586d9fb6f756561d11f74d3209742ef1dcc9daf3fe042087" "q-79316/selection/87d819b585fb71fb451e24c6dd297c8eea938de868d2679b708536cbb2b5f847"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79316" :question/id #uuid "abcaf405-19af-5e04-91a4-4a100842c5a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-79316" :question/problem "A cyclist's remaining distance $R$ to their destination decreases at a rate that's proportional to the time, in minutes, since their journey started. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the cyclist's remaining distance at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*A cyclist's **remaining distance** $R$ to a destination **decreases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **time**, in minutes, since their journey started.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *remaining distance* to a destination varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *time* since their journey started. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-kt.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79316/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection/7e1dc50dca4c97ea88cfec0c97754619da979adc5ec13521b9a128bf317516f0" :answer/id #uuid "42fe3c71-23a7-53ff-bd6e-622ba986ab34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection/60dd874f3df5cc64704af8cb7742d3967be803acf6982eb569f9206199b1813e" :answer/id #uuid "a7f47d35-0b83-5c74-b3b4-3ba60752e64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection/468dcf99a9303f0cd266be5aacdd9f165d173bb1ea34766d371a1a380255f0c5" :answer/id #uuid "51f8e7f5-b543-5151-b6a5-e1edb10f17f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection/aebae903f3fa51d6667dc8c9a211660bb3bf888233a7ef980f6422fe8eb9876d" :answer/id #uuid "b75c7173-c53f-5ebb-973b-4050d1f0febb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection/c10de62d8125dd952ae2853436204c7ac91ef2cf9c24ef921872a8506d65eb0b" :answer/id #uuid "46aadb23-32a7-52ca-8802-5e4bac17e3db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k-\\frac{1}{B},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99d16e8d-cf11-5676-87a1-e8b7d6cc7fb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51254/selection/60dd874f3df5cc64704af8cb7742d3967be803acf6982eb569f9206199b1813e" :answer-field/choices ["q-51254/selection/7e1dc50dca4c97ea88cfec0c97754619da979adc5ec13521b9a128bf317516f0" "q-51254/selection/60dd874f3df5cc64704af8cb7742d3967be803acf6982eb569f9206199b1813e" "q-51254/selection/468dcf99a9303f0cd266be5aacdd9f165d173bb1ea34766d371a1a380255f0c5" "q-51254/selection/aebae903f3fa51d6667dc8c9a211660bb3bf888233a7ef980f6422fe8eb9876d" "q-51254/selection/c10de62d8125dd952ae2853436204c7ac91ef2cf9c24ef921872a8506d65eb0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51254" :question/id #uuid "2cfb46d3-f6f4-5c4b-810e-a81336544d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-51254" :question/problem "The number of bacteria in a particular crop at any given moment decreases at a rate that is proportional to the number of bacteria at that moment.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of bacteria $B$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of bacteria** in a particular crop at any given moment **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to **the number of bacteria** at that moment..* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of bacteria* in a particular crop varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of bacteria* at the moment. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}∝B.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of bacteria *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-51254/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection/44af10799608802758afe727688b835e9a97a32f974e0ba9d21dfd9cbf1776f8" :answer/id #uuid "00d87778-9f6d-572f-ba24-efb2b01987c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k+V,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection/d6eeca2b1359ab9f4498ea8c15d552bb08f531de573038f4bfe94ef9fa3cdd50" :answer/id #uuid "999d8f50-9a49-5221-87cf-61d7ddd7de1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=V" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection/672fef4838b6aabad9763b3add4053ff6bc8e2cc49826cea0c5f3dfdafb1dcc5" :answer/id #uuid "7879ec9f-de30-5298-b5ad-eb700ebabf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=tV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection/5db8bae43c6257d7fd0e44f182d919dbcd1e305159865fa69fe188e0839b6b6e" :answer/id #uuid "12cc5a2f-4920-5e47-b94d-215b9f53fb7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection/c5891dda64aa9e4393b897d75158b0f098c14bb8e02ebdd9f5a11c7a937ec64c" :answer/id #uuid "32a89d93-5177-5162-bd49-ea2e6085aa05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k-V,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d75ca6da-7fe4-5e39-8c9d-57a413cefe1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38589/selection/5db8bae43c6257d7fd0e44f182d919dbcd1e305159865fa69fe188e0839b6b6e" :answer-field/choices ["q-38589/selection/44af10799608802758afe727688b835e9a97a32f974e0ba9d21dfd9cbf1776f8" "q-38589/selection/d6eeca2b1359ab9f4498ea8c15d552bb08f531de573038f4bfe94ef9fa3cdd50" "q-38589/selection/672fef4838b6aabad9763b3add4053ff6bc8e2cc49826cea0c5f3dfdafb1dcc5" "q-38589/selection/5db8bae43c6257d7fd0e44f182d919dbcd1e305159865fa69fe188e0839b6b6e" "q-38589/selection/c5891dda64aa9e4393b897d75158b0f098c14bb8e02ebdd9f5a11c7a937ec64c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38589" :question/id #uuid "1d093bd1-c5c7-53da-bfe8-604b0e2c79b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-38589" :question/problem "Some people in a community contracted an unknown virus. The number of people infected by the virus increases at a rate that is proportional to the number of people infected by the virus. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of people who contracted the virus, $V,$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of people** infected by the virus **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **number of people** infected by the virus.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of people* infected by the virus varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of people* infected. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝V.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of people infected by the virus  *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38589"] :db/ensure [:knowledg