"69c85e0b-7e0b-5837-bb9c-2bbb4965d5f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-38591" :question/problem "When heated, the concentration $C(t)$ of oxygen in water decreases at a rate that's proportional to the concentration of oxygen in the water at that moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the oxygen concentration at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*When heated, the **concentration** $C(t)$ of oxygen in water **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **concentration** of oxygen in the water at that moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *concentration* of oxygen in water varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *concentration* of oxygen in the water. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}∝C.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the concentration of oxygen *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-kC.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection/f3a3a40305179f6dcbd6f09c2ea06965eb3f45f0cd3f6d0021e8a8c8eb241dfe" :answer/id #uuid "1f4cad90-efdf-578b-aa3b-b02ea33b0848" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{H}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection/f7bbaf7d27c02d59fc150831da2577db4ffa51037a582d8fe1f2cf9725dea0df" :answer/id #uuid "78436909-e835-515b-a235-daefd6800f9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection/b101ef23d5dd6a9ea83a348094f34dbedfe6a23555f5f813b64346bba79f8af8" :answer/id #uuid "799ca0c5-0236-59b2-ba0b-012473840cef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection/0e1d23456c8c91d54909f5fc3afde20b3b2e7e40f85c9617bfbcf75ce6fdc3a5" :answer/id #uuid "941ba543-40db-5d41-884c-a1b8163aacce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{H},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection/fafd4998430203cfae35dc7dfebb98b5980a534336116ff3f92242fa9f10f6c4" :answer/id #uuid "a795693e-604f-5700-9d0c-45722f1d2d2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6555f6b-f7fc-58cb-b141-d27d6393ae96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143037/selection/fafd4998430203cfae35dc7dfebb98b5980a534336116ff3f92242fa9f10f6c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-143037/selection/f3a3a40305179f6dcbd6f09c2ea06965eb3f45f0cd3f6d0021e8a8c8eb241dfe" "q-143037/selection/f7bbaf7d27c02d59fc150831da2577db4ffa51037a582d8fe1f2cf9725dea0df" "q-143037/selection/b101ef23d5dd6a9ea83a348094f34dbedfe6a23555f5f813b64346bba79f8af8" "q-143037/selection/0e1d23456c8c91d54909f5fc3afde20b3b2e7e40f85c9617bfbcf75ce6fdc3a5" "q-143037/selection/fafd4998430203cfae35dc7dfebb98b5980a534336116ff3f92242fa9f10f6c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143037" :question/id #uuid "ae491dc9-9063-5d70-aa00-00c9f3a98d29" :question/math-academy-id "q-143037" :question/problem "Construction waste stored in a large pile is taken to a landfill. The height $H$ of the pile decreases with time. The rate of change of the pile's height is proportional to the square of the height. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the height at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of the pile **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the pile's height is **proportional** to the **square of the height**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *height squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝{H}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143037/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection/8d8eddc608f61911e67093ca4b00947b7963d73996423d79e9956f8319091b20" :answer/id #uuid "93ec1bd4-735d-5a6a-9eca-90eeb6de59c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection/c330d08cb16fda35013f1e5c59c0f08fc4b22df601200d4d88ea174a81543c3b" :answer/id #uuid "44752fbb-e7dd-5b05-a2af-d0b0d2fc0056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection/ef34a6f93b84302764f586738065302c25117cc0aaed703930395827152607ac" :answer/id #uuid "3a826549-7c98-5909-a33b-5ca56a8a9db3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection/35419a4fcdc0c7d081a74ef9a6bcc99bc0c668eb693844245fbf58221eae893a" :answer/id #uuid "194579ae-4656-525a-a8b4-ac27ff23406c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection/aa7b68f0db2e4c210acadeb849415c70808abecf8e70f33ab0fe1e786954ffce" :answer/id #uuid "4dd0b829-8111-5c4b-ba12-041c570a3ee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "19d5c9f7-1f25-5e29-95c0-c5ebf4acd9f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143039/selection/c330d08cb16fda35013f1e5c59c0f08fc4b22df601200d4d88ea174a81543c3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-143039/selection/8d8eddc608f61911e67093ca4b00947b7963d73996423d79e9956f8319091b20" "q-143039/selection/c330d08cb16fda35013f1e5c59c0f08fc4b22df601200d4d88ea174a81543c3b" "q-143039/selection/ef34a6f93b84302764f586738065302c25117cc0aaed703930395827152607ac" "q-143039/selection/35419a4fcdc0c7d081a74ef9a6bcc99bc0c668eb693844245fbf58221eae893a" "q-143039/selection/aa7b68f0db2e4c210acadeb849415c70808abecf8e70f33ab0fe1e786954ffce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143039" :question/id #uuid "e05f1f82-64f3-5699-bd01-55ade5a30c00" :question/math-academy-id "q-143039" :question/problem "Mia won some money in the lottery and is now spending it. The amount of money $M$ in her bank account decreases at a rate that's proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in days, since she won.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of money $M$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **amount** of the money $M$ **decreases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in days.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *amount* of money varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the amount *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38313"] :question/problem "A skater is skating straight down a ramp. The displacement $D$ of the skater increases at a rate that's proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in seconds.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of displacement $D$ at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time since he started skating?" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*A skater is skating straight down a ramp. The **displacement** $D$ of the skater **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in seconds. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-51247"] :question/problem "The value $V$ of a particular car decreases with time. The rate of change of the car's value is proportional to the square of the value. What differential equation describes the change of the value at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **value** $V$ of a particular car **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the car's value is **proportional** to the **value squared**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *value* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *value squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝{V}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection/6895bd4ea9af95f7309db096fe43669eab1384e8f2d5bb81ab9bfadbb09eda25" :answer/id #uuid "0c982acd-ce21-51e6-967b-c72097f9f7e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{P},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection/61ef52b081330678825db6121e5b6ecb940db31de850d82e25b6ce3f3fc75fc1" :answer/id #uuid "caa5f777-540e-512d-88e9-a1caf0f4a487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-k{P}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection/75bc157731203d16e828031d15cc17e54bdde376a7b42d2ca8c252dca5a8dca2" :answer/id #uuid "db5d672c-e420-57b6-9f6d-1091901e2cbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{P},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection/c67b23d6a512e841b077c8f76535f026f67376fcbc82a8689078c9baac409f70" :answer/id #uuid "77ed819e-be65-5b39-8395-cc406ecf59ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{P}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection/de8dc191294c47120bac7b09077ff9965e6d6c5e4b4bfd2ec9293ed9ece39a47" :answer/id #uuid "0680a095-bf5c-5423-a0d1-8165cdce2309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k{P}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da764f70-b364-59e6-9be0-62a1bbff0d89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143029/selection/de8dc191294c47120bac7b09077ff9965e6d6c5e4b4bfd2ec9293ed9ece39a47" :answer-field/choices ["q-143029/selection/6895bd4ea9af95f7309db096fe43669eab1384e8f2d5bb81ab9bfadbb09eda25" "q-143029/selection/61ef52b081330678825db6121e5b6ecb940db31de850d82e25b6ce3f3fc75fc1" "q-143029/selection/75bc157731203d16e828031d15cc17e54bdde376a7b42d2ca8c252dca5a8dca2" "q-143029/selection/c67b23d6a512e841b077c8f76535f026f67376fcbc82a8689078c9baac409f70" "q-143029/selection/de8dc191294c47120bac7b09077ff9965e6d6c5e4b4bfd2ec9293ed9ece39a47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143029" :question/id #uuid "f728f48a-b708-5919-9898-226ef8301050" :question/math-academy-id "q-143029" :question/problem "The population $P$ of mosquitos in a particular region increases with time. The rate of change of the population is proportional to the square of the population. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the population of mosquitos at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **population** $P$ of mosquitos **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the population of mosquitos is **proportional** to the **square of the population**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *population* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *population squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}∝{P}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the population *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k{P}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143029/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143029"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection/b96cb125b7dde3a9bad6848acc09c871db0c13c6cf2b5c7d1aec9076d5c30585" :answer/id #uuid "042ca691-6da5-522d-9381-8c694df7c921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-kC,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection/4eeed4cfff9fba8c7ce404a5cf4fbdd9fad79cd2f10ada32113ce6f07fc54832" :answer/id #uuid "6574d030-f380-59b8-aa8b-254c8f43b957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{C},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection/db0eafac5ee1c9c8ad58a8c88b5cc9bd3373832865d667b6e3bcbb58f28b61f2" :answer/id #uuid "c1bc5056-30f6-5a25-a4fb-b5a739b891e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection/19106f6f1b697699d9a40c8371609a982c03fb4d67c0acaa93c38456abf0754f" :answer/id #uuid "f4cf587d-db87-57e5-9a06-a4b3afa3e174" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection/4304ddbcf2013e4ee2749f4442b4831a75aea9d4535019b12f5bfc365fbe1552" :answer/id #uuid "b5d87430-9de6-50b0-a49f-c9df03b20297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35de313a-7ad5-57b8-9455-ebbcd948f70c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143081/selection/db0eafac5ee1c9c8ad58a8c88b5cc9bd3373832865d667b6e3bcbb58f28b61f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-143081/selection/b96cb125b7dde3a9bad6848acc09c871db0c13c6cf2b5c7d1aec9076d5c30585" "q-143081/selection/4eeed4cfff9fba8c7ce404a5cf4fbdd9fad79cd2f10ada32113ce6f07fc54832" "q-143081/selection/db0eafac5ee1c9c8ad58a8c88b5cc9bd3373832865d667b6e3bcbb58f28b61f2" "q-143081/selection/19106f6f1b697699d9a40c8371609a982c03fb4d67c0acaa93c38456abf0754f" "q-143081/selection/4304ddbcf2013e4ee2749f4442b4831a75aea9d4535019b12f5bfc365fbe1552"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143081" :question/id #uuid "f6d27ee8-7a9e-59cc-aba5-99cecf01eb5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143081" :question/problem "The charge $C$ of a phone battery decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the time $t$ spent charging the smartphone. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the charge $C$ of the phone battery?" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **charge** $C$ of a phone battery **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **time** $t$ spent charging the smartphone.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *charge* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{t}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143081/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143081"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection/fe38b9f5a2dd2970d848d646592a7f793d47cf088b97bd7cda45d3edfdeba56b" :answer/id #uuid "3815e13d-52cc-566d-8290-274d1e7a3f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection/245c4738191f69406d13e6eaf7e1348dfb26525aaf236e1a9be19398644872a0" :answer/id #uuid "9dcd7858-cbe0-5076-8b17-8092abaf53a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection/1bab157f8450169e52b13ca93c531510c24f26ca98f5b3019bc4d042976c89f5" :answer/id #uuid "9160920f-9320-5c23-a35b-5ff41cbc2b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection/9fd454d63ceb1aa37135b56be1697688d96f4c6c4a4462f9b350f0e06b66644d" :answer/id #uuid "8fbac362-195b-5db7-b1fb-57506ad7b25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection/03c720fb896a9cb7230df755687c17181f3c819b7dff6bead38b36a46544aacb" :answer/id #uuid "ab0a2484-9701-5ebf-9683-ac60974c8b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "088bf1a8-a840-5d18-8346-7195ea4d0130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143094/selection/fe38b9f5a2dd2970d848d646592a7f793d47cf088b97bd7cda45d3edfdeba56b" :answer-field/choices ["q-143094/selection/fe38b9f5a2dd2970d848d646592a7f793d47cf088b97bd7cda45d3edfdeba56b" "q-143094/selection/245c4738191f69406d13e6eaf7e1348dfb26525aaf236e1a9be19398644872a0" "q-143094/selection/1bab157f8450169e52b13ca93c531510c24f26ca98f5b3019bc4d042976c89f5" "q-143094/selection/9fd454d63ceb1aa37135b56be1697688d96f4c6c4a4462f9b350f0e06b66644d" "q-143094/selection/03c720fb896a9cb7230df755687c17181f3c819b7dff6bead38b36a46544aacb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143094" :question/id #uuid "d4f83b6d-0b59-5cc8-9341-b97fb9c62549" :question/math-academy-id "q-143094" :question/problem "The speed $S$ of an object decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the travel time $t.$ What differential equation describes the rate of change of the speed $S?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **speed** $S$ of an object **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the travel time** $t.$*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *speed* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the travel time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the speed *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143094/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143094"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143061/selection/2dd14c48364fc984012cf94e6f61bccb3ac897037eafd855113f2822b364ad22" :answer/id #uuid "346ee82a-dcbd-51a0-8153-38d4acb62d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143061/selection/be41d3a3545cead642d5362afde9e09f959182c1fc814a2918b3bd2f59046e50" :answer/id #uuid "9690b205-4f85-5ab2-a542-6fadb7cff0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143061/selection/b80a600fa0639259c483e8a6ba