 in the given statement:\n\n*The  **volume of water** $V$  in a pool being filled **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the ** square of the volume of water** $V$ in the pool at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of water* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the volume.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of water *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143061/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143061"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143078/selection/d5008f21ea71d14029585d7af51d969b9ae35d6131378312b4501d83c478d7d3" :answer/id #uuid "262ed2c0-4675-5f4b-819a-9fb07c163489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143078/selection/17374244857ab8a9701babbef1b0bf8ad6828495f088c5661ad1d15e014af50b" :answer/id #uuid "24f3b892-f7f6-558e-81f6-37d50c51bdc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=-k{I}^{2},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143078/selection/cc46f72990b82b6132bec761f87fefdefa1fa793e7ce1819822e5c2ee9905079" :answer/id #uuid "d3a3e563-63ee-5583-a682-83a1701e6594" :answer/type :answer.typ